ally  wonderful experience having just come  off a big studio film  to work on an independent film where i  was doing everything  and it really helped me kind of  recalibrate  how important it is sometimes we get  removed from the set  as costume designers since we're always  you know we're technically an offset  position  or we get removed from the making of a  costume  so this was is such a memorable film for  me because i was able to  kind of be involved in all aspects of  the  um costumes from creation to being on  set  and this is mike potter the genius wig  designer and  makeup artist who created hedwig's look  from day one  from the nightclubs of new york city to  off-broadway hedwig  to the film he was my partner  in um you know crime and  we were yeah the costume is really only  completed by the wig and makeup and we  really really worked  closely i don't think i've ever worked  so intimately  with another hair and makeup artist so  that was  really thrilling that we were able to  kind of create these looks  together with different wigs that's  mike again mike potter who played a  little guest role  as a prostitute in the meatpacking  district a male prostitute male drag  prostitute in the meat packing district  but and i think he's in  partial makeup there  and mike potter again um he  is uh modeling hedwig's  sunglasses that we see in the beginning  of the movie  he was my muse as well  and mike potter doing hair for one of  the  head heads which are hedwig's groupies  this is paul who is actually a long time  friend of  john cameron mitchell john had a lot of  his friends play different parts in the  movie it was a real family atmosphere  this is michael pitt who  in a fitting for tommy nosis one of his  performance  costumes and michael was incredible to  work with  another tommynosis costume fitting with  michael pitt  and another one i don't think that made  the cut  and this is a photo of michael pitt on  set  for that trailer park scene and um  i lo